  "interpretation": "The repeated vacuum yaw pulses show a mean absolute roll/yaw acceleration ratio of 0.385. The full-vessel inertia predicts 0.036 for a pure body-z yaw torque, about 10.7 times smaller. The captured off-diagonal inertia alone does not explain the cross-axis response. Applying the full three-axis Euler relation to the measured slopes implies an input-correlated body-roll torque of about 3.1% of the yaw torque in both pulse directions; this is inferred net torque, not a direct wheel measurement, and its actuator source remains unresolved. The independent native vessel-frame pulse gives a ratio of 0.379, with quaternion and SpaceCenter.transform_direction rates agreeing within 8.29e-09 rad/s. The earlier probe's body_rates helper negates the native right-handed vector, so its inferred torque signs are reversed; magnitudes and ratios are unchanged. Using native signs, the inferred roll/yaw moments are about 95/3150 N\u00b7m for the positive pulse and 94/3043 N\u00b7m for the negative pulse. These remain inferred net moments; the actuator source is unresolved. This is not atmospheric coordination or flight qualification.",
  "sourceSHA256": "0994ce398c8ff16a743c026e7ced039f1520b027a9079eddbc984fa4be85ef71"
